                    <!-- 📋 Part 1: What Are Menus? -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; border-left: 6px solid #4facfe;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4facfe 0%, #00f2fe 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-1 me-2"></i>What Are Menus?</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <div class="alert alert-info">
                                    <i class="fas fa-question-circle me-2"></i>
                                    <strong>In Simple Words:</strong> Menus are like <strong>restaurant menus</strong>
                                    for your app - they show users what they can do and help them find features quickly!
                                </div>

                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-utensils text-primary me-2"></i>🍽️ Real-World Analogy</h5>
                                                <p><strong>Think of menus like a restaurant menu:</strong></p>
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li>📋 <strong>Menu Bar</strong> = The menu categories (Appetizers, Main Course, Desserts)</li>
                                                    <li>📄 <strong>Menu Items</strong> = The actual dishes (File → Open, File → Save)</li>
                                                    <li>⌨️ <strong>Shortcuts</strong> = "Today's Special" (Ctrl+S, Ctrl+O)</li>
                                                    <li>🔀 <strong>Submenus</strong> = Sub-categories (Edit → Find → Find Next)</li>
                                                </ul>
                                                <div class="alert alert-success mt-2">
                                                    <i class="fas fa-check-circle me-2"></i>
                                                    <strong>Result:</strong> Users can easily find what they need!
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-code text-primary me-2"></i>💻 Common Menu Structure</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="comment">// Typical menu structure in Windows apps</span>
File
    ├── New        (Ctrl+N)
    ├── Open       (Ctrl+O)
    ├── Save       (Ctrl+S)
    ├── ─────────  (Separator)
    └── Exit       (Alt+F4)

Edit
    ├── Undo       (Ctrl+Z)
    ├── Redo       (Ctrl+Y)
    ├── ─────────
    ├── Cut        (Ctrl+X)
    ├── Copy       (Ctrl+C)
    └── Paste      (Ctrl+V)

Help
    └── About</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                                <p><span class="badge bg-primary">📌</span> Every professional app has menus!</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="card bg-warning text-dark mt-3">
                                    <div class="card-body">
                                        <i class="fas fa-laugh-beam me-2"></i>
                                        <strong>😂 Fun Joke:</strong> Why did the menu go to the doctor?
                                        Because it had too many items! (Get it? Menu items? ...I'll stop 😅)
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- 🛠️ Part 2: Creating a Menu -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; border-left: 6px solid #43e97b;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43e97b 0%, #38f9d7 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-2 me-2"></i>Creating a Menu</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-code text-primary me-2"></i>📝 Step-by-Step</h5>
                                                <ol>
                                                    <li><strong>Add MenuStrip</strong> - From Toolbox, drag <code>MenuStrip</code> to your form</li>
                                                    <li><strong>Add Top-Level Menus</strong> - Type "File", "Edit", "Help"</li>
                                                    <li><strong>Add Menu Items</strong> - Click the arrow and type item names</li>
                                                    <li><strong>Add Separators</strong> - Type a dash "-" to add a line</li>
                                                    <li><strong>Add Shortcuts</strong> - In Properties, set <code>ShortcutKeys</code></li>
                                                </ol>
                                                <div class="card bg-info text-white mt-2">
                                                    <div class="card-body">
                                                        <i class="fas fa-lightbulb me-2"></i>
                                                        <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Type "&amp;File" to make Alt+F work (the &amp; underlines the F)!
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-play text-success me-2"></i>🎯 Example: File Menu</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="comment">// Creating a menu in code</span>
<span class="class">MenuStrip</span> menuStrip = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">MenuStrip</span>();

<span class="comment">// Create File menu</span>
<span class="class">ToolStripMenuItem</span> fileMenu = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">ToolStripMenuItem</span>(<span class="string">"&amp;File"</span>);
<span class="class">ToolStripMenuItem</span> newItem = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">ToolStripMenuItem</span>(<span class="string">"&amp;New"</span>, <span class="keyword">null</span>, <span class="function">New_Click</span>);
newItem.ShortcutKeys = Keys.Control | Keys.N;

fileMenu.DropDownItems.Add(newItem);
menuStrip.Items.Add(fileMenu);
<span class="keyword">this</span>.MainMenuStrip = menuStrip;</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                                <p><span class="badge bg-success">✨</span> Designer is easier - just type the menu names!</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="card bg-warning text-dark mt-3">
                                    <div class="card-body">
                                        <i class="fas fa-lightbulb me-2"></i>
                                        <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Use <strong>&amp;</strong> before a letter to create an access key (Alt+Letter).
                                        Example: "&amp;File" = Alt+F opens the File menu!
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- 🖥️ Part 3: Common Dialogs -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="300">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; border-left: 6px solid #f093fb;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f093fb 0%, #f5576c 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-3 me-2"></i>Common Dialogs</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <div class="alert alert-info">
                                    <i class="fas fa-question-circle me-2"></i>
                                    <strong>What are Dialogs?</strong> Dialogs are <strong>pop-up windows</strong>
                                    that help users perform specific tasks like opening files, saving files, or choosing colors.
                                </div>

                                <div class="table-responsive">
                                    <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                                        <thead class="table-dark">
                                            <tr>
                                                <th>Dialog</th>
                                                <th>What It Does</th>
                                                <th>How to Use</th>
                                            </tr>
                                        </thead>
                                        <tbody>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td><strong>OpenFileDialog</strong></td>
                                                <td>User chooses a file to open</td>
                                                <td>File → Open</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td><strong>SaveFileDialog</strong></td>
                                                <td>User chooses where to save</td>
                                                <td>File → Save As</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td><strong>FolderBrowserDialog</strong></td>
                                                <td>User chooses a folder</td>
                                                <td>Tools → Options</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td><strong>ColorDialog</strong></td>
                                                <td>User picks a color</td>
                                                <td>Format → Color</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td><strong>FontDialog</strong></td>
                                                <td>User picks a font</td>
                                                <td>Format → Font</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td><strong>PrintDialog</strong></td>
                                                <td>User chooses print options</td>
                                                <td>File → Print</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td><strong>MessageBox</strong></td>
                                                <td>Shows messages to users</td>
                                                <td>Anywhere!</td>
                                            </tr>
                                        </tbody>
                                    </table>
                                </div>

                                <div class="card bg-success text-white mt-3">
                                    <div class="card-body">
                                        <i class="fas fa-laugh-beam me-2"></i>
                                        <strong>😂 Fun Fact:</strong> The most used dialog in WinForms is the <strong>MessageBox</strong> -
                                        it's the "Are you sure?" king!
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- 📂 Part 4: Open File Dialog -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="400">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; border-left: 6px solid #667eea;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-4 me-2"></i>Open File Dialog - Let Users Choose Files</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-code text-primary me-2"></i>📝 Using OpenFileDialog</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="keyword">private void</span> <span class="function">openToolStripMenuItem_Click</span>(<span class="keyword">object</span> sender, <span class="class">EventArgs</span> e)
{
    <span class="comment">// Create and configure the dialog</span>
    <span class="keyword">using</span> (<span class="class">OpenFileDialog</span> openFileDialog = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">OpenFileDialog</span>())
    {
        openFileDialog.Title = <span class="string">"Select a file to open"</span>;
        openFileDialog.Filter = <span class="string">"Text Files (*.txt)|*.txt|All Files (*.*)|*.*"</span>;
        openFileDialog.FilterIndex = <span class="number">1</span>;
        openFileDialog.RestoreDirectory = <span class="keyword">true</span>;
        
        <span class="comment">// Show the dialog and check if user clicked OK</span>
        <span class="keyword">if</span> (openFileDialog.ShowDialog() == <span class="class">DialogResult</span>.OK)
        {
            <span class="comment">// Read the selected file</span>
            <span class="keyword">string</span> content = <span class="class">File</span>.<span class="function">ReadAllText</span>(openFileDialog.FileName);
            txtContent.Text = content;
            lblStatus.Text = <span class="string">$"Loaded: {openFileDialog.FileName}"</span>;
        }
    }
}</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>✅ Common Properties</h5>
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li><strong>Filter</strong> - What files to show (e.g., "*.txt")</li>
                                                    <li><strong>Title</strong> - Dialog window title</li>
                                                    <li><strong>FileName</strong> - The selected file path</li>
                                                    <li><strong>RestoreDirectory</strong> - Remember last folder</li>
                                                    <li><strong>Multiselect</strong> - Allow selecting multiple files</li>
                                                </ul>
                                                <div class="card bg-info text-white mt-2">
                                                    <div class="card-body">
                                                        <i class="fas fa-lightbulb me-2"></i>
                                                        <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Always use <code>using</code> with file dialogs
                                                        to ensure resources are properly disposed!
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="card bg-warning text-dark mt-3">
                                    <div class="card-body">
                                        <i class="fas fa-laugh-beam me-2"></i>
                                        <strong>😂 Joke:</strong> Why did the file open?
                                        Because it heard there was a dialog! (Bad pun, I know 😅)
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- 💾 Part 5: Save File Dialog -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="500">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; border-left: 6px solid #43e97b;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43e97b 0%, #38f9d7 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-5 me-2"></i>Save File Dialog - Save User Data</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-code text-primary me-2"></i>📝 Using SaveFileDialog</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="keyword">private void</span> <span class="function">saveToolStripMenuItem_Click</span>(<span class="keyword">object</span> sender, <span class="class">EventArgs</span> e)
{
    <span class="keyword">using</span> (<span class="class">SaveFileDialog</span> saveFileDialog = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="class">SaveFileDialog</span>())
    {
        saveFileDialog.Title = <span class="string">"Save your work"</span>;
        saveFileDialog.Filter = <span class="string">"Text Files (*.txt)|*.txt|All Files (*.*)|*.*"</span>;
        saveFileDialog.DefaultExt = <span class="string">"txt"</span>;
        
        <span class="keyword">if</span> (saveFileDialog.ShowDialog() == <span class="class">DialogResult</span>.OK)
        {
            <span class="comment">// Save the content</span>
            <span class="class">File</span>.<span class="function">WriteAllText</span>(saveFileDialog.FileName, txtContent.Text);
            lblStatus.Text = <span class="string">$"Saved: {saveFileDialog.FileName}"</span>;
            <span class="class">MessageBox</span>.<span class="function">Show</span>(<span class="string">"File saved successfully!"</span>, <span class="string">"Success"</span>);
        }
    }
}</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>✅ Common Properties</h5>
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li><strong>Filter</strong> - File types to show</li>
                                                    <li><strong>DefaultExt</strong> - Default file extension</li>
                                                    <li><strong>FileName</strong> - The chosen file path</li>
                                                    <li><strong>OverwritePrompt</strong> - Ask before overwriting</li>
                                                    <li><strong>AddExtension</strong> - Add extension automatically</li>
                                                </ul>
                                                <div class="card bg-warning text-dark mt-2">
                                                    <div class="card-body">
                                                        <i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle me-2"></i>
                                                        <strong>Warning:</strong> Always check if the user clicked OK before saving!
                                                        Use <code>if (saveFileDialog.ShowDialog() == DialogResult.OK)</code>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- 💬 Part 6: MessageBox - The "Are You Sure?" King -->
                    <section class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="600">
                        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg" style="border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; border-left: 6px solid #f093fb;">
                            <div class="card-header" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f093fb 0%, #f5576c 100%); color: white; border: none;">
                                <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-6 me-2"></i>MessageBox - The "Are You Sure?" King</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body p-4">
                                <div class="alert alert-info">
                                    <i class="fas fa-comment me-2"></i>
                                    <strong>What is MessageBox?</strong> The most common dialog - it <strong>shows messages</strong>
                                    to users and can ask for <strong>simple input</strong> (Yes/No, OK/Cancel).
                                </div>

                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-code text-primary me-2"></i>📝 MessageBox Examples</h5>
                                                <div class="code-block small">
                                                    <pre><code class="language-csharp"><span class="comment">// Simple message</span>
<span class="class">MessageBox</span>.<span class="function">Show</span>(<span class="string">"Hello World!"</span>);

<span class="comment">// With title</span>
<span class="class">MessageBox</span>.<span class="function">Show</span>(<span class="string">"Data saved!"</span>, <span class="string">"Success"</span>);

<span class="comment">// With icon</span>
<span class="class">MessageBox</span>.<span class="function">Show</span>(<span class="string">"An error occurred"</span>, <span class="string">"Error"</span>, 
    <span class="class">MessageBoxButtons</span>.OK, <span class="class">MessageBoxIcon</span>.Error);

<span class="comment">// Ask Yes/No question</span>
<span class="class">DialogResult</span> result = <span class="class">MessageBox</span>.<span class="function">Show</span>(<span class="string">"Are you sure?"</span>, 
    <span class="string">"Confirm"</span>, <span class="class">MessageBoxButtons</span>.YesNo);

<span class="keyword">if</span> (result == <span class="class">DialogResult</span>.Yes)
{
    <span class="comment">// User clicked Yes</span>
}</code></pre>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-lg-6">
                                        <div class="card bg-light h-100">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <h5><i class="fas fa-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>✅ MessageBox Options</h5>
                                                <div class="table-responsive">
                                                    <table class="table table-bordered table-sm">
                                                        <thead class="table-dark">
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <th>Buttons</th>
                                                                <th>Icons</th>
                                                            </tr>
                                                        </thead>
                                                        <tbody>
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td>OK</td>
                                                                <td>Information</td>
                                                            </tr>
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td>OKCancel</td>
                                                                <td>Warning</td>
                                                            </tr>
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td>YesNo</td>
                                                                <td>Error</td>
                                                            </tr>
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td>YesNoCancel</td>
                                                                <td>Question</td>
                                                            </tr>
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td>AbortRetryIgnore</td>
                                                                <td>Exclamation</td>
                                                            </tr>
                                                        </tbody>
                                                    </table>
                                                </div>
                                                <div class="card bg-success text-white mt-2">
                                                    <div class="card-body">
                                                        <i class="fas fa-laugh-beam me-2"></i>
                                                        <strong>😂 Fun Fact:</strong> MessageBox is so common that
                                                        some developers use it for debugging instead of Console.WriteLine!
